arrow shape into a displayed vector;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:37:  - The arrow silhouettes are intentionally chunky and asymmetric, so humans can read them\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:55:    3. the dominant legend-color mask matches one of the 5x5/6x7 arrow templates;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:65:  - Humans can first read the left arrow in the usual way, then compare it to the right arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:66:  - Right-colored rooms visibly disobey their own displayed arrow and instead follow the vector\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:79:  - Color 1 is just a legend plate color; all nontrivial inference comes from arrow orientation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:83:  - Metric: compare the combo output against a legacy-arrow output that incorrectly lets the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:84:    second wall color follow its own displayed arrow directly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:90:  - main() assumes the dominant legend color is the wall color; generator uses masks where the arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:171:def _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:176:def _diagonal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:188:CARDINAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in CARDINAL_DIRS}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:189:DIAGONAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _diagonal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in DIAGONAL_DIRS}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/code.py:194:    patch[_cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc)] = fill\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/20/cod