ugh for ARC-style reasoning.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/17/code.py:34:   - Marker geometry is also narrow: a short 1xk or kx1 segment outside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:3:# Name: 统一轴向射线+形状决定距离+箭头精灵\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:21:#   - Every sprite is now a 3-pixel arrow that points directly along one of the 4 cardinal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:24:#     encoded by arrow family:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:25:#       * kind \"L\": skew hook arrow, range 4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:26:#       * kind \"V\": symmetric chevron arrow, range 6\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:29:#       * fused analogue can be a short-range up arrow {(5,5),(6,4),(6,5)}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:31:#       * a long-range up arrow {(5,5),(6,4),(6,6)} points the same way but lands at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:32:#         (-1,5) conceptually, so the generator only places such arrows where tip+6*dir stays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:34:#         arrow silhouette plus the induced landing distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:36:#   - The fusion is not simplified into a single arrow template: there are two reusable shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:41:#   - Generator examples force both arrow families to appear and reject cases whose output is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:45:#     monochrome, 8-connected arrow matching exactly one template. The generator uses only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:46:#     those templates and validates them with _arrow_info(...).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:50:#     _arrow_info returns only those labels, and generator placements are precomputed by kind.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:54:#   - Placements are precomputed only when both the arrow cells and tip+range*dir destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:59:#   - All arrows are axis-aligned, so the D1 change is visible directly in the input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:60:#   - The two arrow silhouettes are visually distinct, and both appear repeatedly, so the D2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:66:#   - No rule depends on hidden ordering or color ranking; only local shape family, arrow tip,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:111:def _arrow_info(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:114:    \"\"\"Return (tip_rc, dir_rc, kind) for a 3-cell axis arrow sprite, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:147:        info = _arrow_info(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:177:    Fire straight projectiles from 3-pixel arrow sprites, with range determined by arrow family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:180:    - The background is the most common color, and each foreground component is a 3-cell monochrome arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:181:    - Every arrow points directly up, down, left, or right from a single tip cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:182:    - There are two arrow silhouettes: a skew hook family and a symmetric chevron family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:185:    - Read the firing direction from the arrow tip itself; all projectiles travel along cardinal rays only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:186:    - The arrow family sets the distance: hook arrows (the former L-coded family) travel 4 cells, while chevron arrows (the former V-coded family) travel 6 cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:191:    - Direction has become visually explicit, so the remaining inference is to separate the two arrow families and notice that they keep different fixed ranges even though they shoot along the same four axes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/8/code.py:319:    return all(_arrow_info(comp) is not None for comp in comps)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/8/code.py:28:#    The topology family is still narrow enough that 2-4 examples support the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:33:       a left token drops through 6, while under the old narrow-gate rule it would have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:39:     The generator therefore enforces at least two wide gates and at least two narrow gates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:42:     every wide gate as narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:66:     bars, and the corresponding output rows show narrow vs wide opened passages around the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:68:   - Because accepted samples must differ from the \"all narrow\" baseline, the width signal is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:383:def _baseline_narrow_gates(gates: list[list[tuple[int, int]]]) -> list[list[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:460:    baseline_opened = _build_opened_grid(_baseline_narrow_gates(gates), width)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:471:    enriched_stats[\"narrow_gates\"] = int(sum(span == NARROW for row in gates for _center, span in row))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:473:    enriched_stats[\"diff_vs_narrow\"] = int(np.count_nonzero(fused_out != baseline_out))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:496:    if int(stats[\"narrow_gates\"]) < 2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/21/code.py:506:    if int(stats[\"diff_vs_narrow\"]) < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/48/code.py:16:#      a pair of narrow lower shafts that can catch falling liquid. The fused palette is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/48/code.py:33:#    - The color freedom is intentionally narrow. Using exactly two fresh colors plus one old\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/48/code.py:36:#    - The geometry is also narrow: both fresh sources feed into two one-cell-wide shafts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/48/code.py:71:#      narrow liquid shafts. No legends or overlapping annotations are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/27/code.py:75:  reasoning space narrow and readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/22/code.py:40:#    - Original assumption: a gate row may have 0-3 gates. The combo narrows this to exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/4/code.py:51:    column), which keeps the visual language narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/20/code.py:58:#    narrow, so the output reads as maroon spread through many triangles plus a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/8/code.py:69:#     narrower rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/16/code.py:55:#    - The crop is equally visible because outputs are narrower and shorter than the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/12/code.py:31:#    The layout family is intentionally narrow: three cups, one lower source roof, and only five\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:3:# Name: 图例顺序编码方向加箭头图例\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:37:#    The obstacle family stays narrow and readable: 3-4 solid edge bars, 2-4 cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:162:    arrow_patch = mask[_ARROW_ROWS, _ARROW_COLS]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:164:        if np.array_equal(arrow_patch, template):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:166:    raise AssertionError(f\"unrecognized legend arrow patch:\\n{arrow_patch.astype(int)}\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:292:    \"\"\"Build the fixed 6x24 legend band using swatches plus mirrored elbow arrows.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:572:    Trace legend-ordered teal rays whose turn rules come from arrow glyphs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/21/code.py:595:    arrow glyph gives each obstacle color's turn direction, and the visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/22/code.py:191:    - Process foreground colors in priority order by compactness: clean the narrow reference color first by the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头精灵+方向由最近边缘决定\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:18:#    The visible sprites are now 3-pixel arrows in 8 compass facings, so the input suggests\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:19:#    \"follow the arrow tip\". The fusion rule breaks that expectation: the tip still marks the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:22:#      cells {(3,6),(4,5),(4,6)} form a NE-looking arrow with tip (3,6).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:28:#      fires upward to an in-bounds cell even though the arrow still visually points NE.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:33:#    - Keep exactly 8 arrow templates and exactly 4 actual firing directions (toward top/bottom/\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:35:#    - Require both diagonal-looking and axis-looking arrows in each generated grid; otherwise the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:37:#    - Require repeated evidence that arrows are misleading: several sprites must fire in a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:43:#      combo, only emitter recovery survives, and it must be replaced by arrow-template matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:51:#    - Generation precomputes all arrow placements whose 3 cells are in bounds, whose nearest edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:55:#    - Under this toward-edge geometry, legal 5-step destinations stay in narrow border bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:61:#    - The crucial observable is disagreement between arrow facing and actual shot direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:63:#      arrow\" solver on the same input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:65:#      arrow facings within at least one shared nearest-edge class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:78:#    - For each sprite, compare `visual_dir` from the arrow template with `actual_dir` from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:84:#    - Every non-bg component is exactly one 3-pixel arrow matching a unique template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:85:#    - Every generated arrow has a unique nearest edge; ties are excluded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:86:#    - The projectile always starts from the arrow tip, not from any other pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:138:def _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:175:def _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:180:    tip_data = _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:193:    Fire projectiles from 3-pixel arrow sprites, but aim them by border proximity instead of arrow facing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:197:    - Every non-background 8-connected component is a monochrome 3-pixel arrow in one of 8 visual facings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:198:    - The arrow tip still identifies the launch cell, but the arrow's pointing direction is not the movement rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:201:    - Match each component to an arrow template to recover its tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:206:    Key insight: The arrowhead is a red herring. Shape tells you where the shot starts, but the shot direction comes from the sprite's global position relative to the border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:223:        td = _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(comp, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:267:        td = _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:429:        if _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(coords, H, W) is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/31/code.py:64:  wide enough to be seen by eye, narrow enough that the frame grid still reads as one object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/_logs/launch_meta.json:255:    \"name\": \"图例顺序编码方向加箭头图例\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/_logs/launch_meta.json:448:    \"name\": \"箭头图例双参数编码可变角度\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/36/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头图例双参数编码可变角度\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/36/code.py:10:      - replace each legend bar with a bottom-aligned colored hook / arrow token inside a 4x4 black cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/29/code.py:64:    Key insight: The separator spacing reveals the slot-grid dimensions, but the occupied extent of the top-band shapes reveals the narrower template width; marker locality and marker color must be decoded separately.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/24/code.py:80:    Key insight: Color still narrows the choice to a template group, but repeated colors are resolved by visible marker frequency, while the marker's local position still encodes the output block location.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/15/code.py:43:#   - The long-approach change is kept in a narrow range: obstacle md 5-12, mostly produced by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/18/code.py:478:    \"\"\"Carve a narrow background fjord from the left edge without disconnecting the path.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/8/code.py:354:        raise ValueError(\"grid too narrow for dependency corridor\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/16/code.py:67:#     - Payload cells lie on a narrow ring around the cross, so the local geometry\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/1/code.py:544:    \"\"\"Carve a narrow bg separator from the left edge without disconnecting path.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/21/code.py:40:#    - Object count is narrowed to exactly 4 (a 2x2 frame grid). This keeps the legend short and lets frame colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/11/code.py:66:#     To keep the task solvable, the generator narrows the rectangle size and piece\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:21:#   - Width is restricted to the small visible set {2, 3}; that is narrow enough\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:33:#     non-background population. The generator keeps the narrow band dominant over\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:481:    \"\"\"Stable 15x15 narrow-band layout with a readable left-edge separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头头部对准目标点\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:20:# - The head is no longer a full edge line. It is a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:26:#   in the arrow's pointing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:27:# - The translation distance is measured from the arrow tip to the point, not from arrow bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:28:#   top-left and not from a full line center. After moving k steps, the arrow tip advances by k and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:33:#   D4/2 alone: an arrow attached on the left may still point down, so direction comes from shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:35:#   Combo here: an arrow attached orthogonally to the motion axis points toward a single dot, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:36:#   the arrow tip rather than any bbox anchor is what aligns to that dot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:37:#   Example: a right-pointing arrow attached above the container has tip at (r, c). A point sits at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:42:# - The arrow vocabulary is still only four shapes, keeping shape parsing low-entropy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:43:# - To ensure this is visibly different from the source task, the generator only attaches arrows on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:46:# - The target is always a point with at least one background cell between it and the arrow tip, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:51:#   Broken. In the combo, the arrow may be above the box while motion is right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:55:#   top-left. Broken again: a point has no meaningful shared shape anchor with the arrow. The new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:56:#   anchor is the arrow tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:58:#   between arrow tip and point. The solver still contains a tiny fallback for malformed gap=0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:59:#   inputs by trying to peel one extra pixel off an otherwise valid arrow component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:62:# - Each generated assembly reserves the union of five regions: input container, input arrow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:63:#   destination point, moved container, moved arrow. Packing is done with a 1-cell background moat.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:68:# - Across samples, the arrow is visibly not on the side of travel, forcing the solver to read its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:73:# - Only three foreground object types appear: bordered container, arrow head, point target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:74:#   The point is sparse, the arrow is compact, and assemblies are separated by background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:78:#   direction, so the only new inference burden is the fused geometry: arrow orientation + tip to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:82:# - Head components are exact 3x3 arrow sprites, or that sprite plus one fused forward point in the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:84:# - Every mover has exactly one nearest forward point on its arrow ray; the generator verifies\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:86:# - Motion direction, fill order, and point alignment are all keyed off the arrow direction, not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:147:def _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h: int, outer_w: int, attach_side: str, anchor: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/7/code.py:157:def _stamp_arrow(grid: 