ust point to an ambient path cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:46:#   arrows remain separate 8-connected components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:52:# - Humans can see two independent cues in the input: arrow orientation decides the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:54:# - The generator requires at least one arrow whose decoded heading differs from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:67:# - There are 1-2 arrow markers, each an 8-connected size-3 component matching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:68:#   exactly one arrowhead orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:105:def _arrow_cells(tip_r: int, tip_c: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:109:def _decode_arrow_component(coords: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int, str] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:110:    \"\"\"Return (tip_r, tip_c, direction) for a 3-cell arrowhead component.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:117:            if set(_arrow_cells(int(tip_r), int(tip_c), direction)) == comp:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:182:def _find_arrow_markers(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:185:    \"\"\"Find 3-cell arrow markers whose colors belong to the decoded cycle.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:192:            decoded = _decode_arrow_component(coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:211:def _assert_arrow_markers_valid(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:217:    assert 1 <= len(markers) <= 2, f\"expected 1-2 arrow markers, got {len(markers)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:221:        assert tuple(sorted(_arrow_cells(tip_r, tip_c, direction))) == cells, (\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:295:    - Start markers are 3-cell arrowheads in template colors, embedded inside the path region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:300:    - Each arrow launches one particle from its tip in the direction encoded by the arrowhead shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:304:    Key insight: The path dynamics are still the original alternating-turn walk, but the input now hides two independent controls in local geometry: arrow shape chooses the initial heading, and corner-template shape chooses the usable cycle order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:333:    markers = _find_arrow_markers(g, pattern, path_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:334:    _assert_arrow_markers_valid(g, markers, path_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:494:def _collect_arrow_candidates(mask: np.ndarray, target_row: int) -> list[dict[str, object]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:508:                    cells = _arrow_cells(int(r), int(c), direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:547:def _place_arrow_markers(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:553:    cand_lists = [_collect_arrow_candidates(mask, int(row)) for row in target_rows]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:599:    # Right-pointing arrows are structurally rarer because they usually agree\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:601:    # legal pair containing one R arrow while still requiring another\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:602:    # interesting arrow, so D4 remains observable and direction branches stay covered.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:715:    placed = _place_arrow_markers(g, mask, target_rows, marker_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/9/code.py:20:#   The family is intentionally narrow: one frame, 2 or 3 tools, strictly decreasing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:3:# Name: 内部图案决定方向加箭头头部\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:21:# - Outside the container there is now a 3x3 maroon arrow head plus a matching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:22:#   3x3 maroon destination arrow further along the travel direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:25:#     2. Use the external arrow only as the movable head sprite and as a visual\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:27:# - To make that visible, the head arrow is always attached on a side orthogonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:30:#     * internal orange cells form a right-pointing arrow template\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:31:#     * external arrow head also points right, but it is attached above or below\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:34:#       destination arrow to the right of the source arrow, then move container\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:38:#     * fused: internal orange arrow decides direction, head position is decoupled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:39:#       from direction, and the head itself is a compact arrow sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:43:# - The internal cue is a fixed 4-cell arrow template, not an arbitrary shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:44:# - The external cue is a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:53:#   still keep its identity. Broken: a 3x3 arrow must be tracked as a full shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:55:#   must depend on the internal arrow direction instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:56:# - New assumption introduced here: movers have a unique internal arrow template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:60:# - New assumption introduced here: the external arrow direction agrees with the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:61:#   internal arrow direction. Generator guarantees this and solver checks it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:65:#     input container, input head arrow, destination arrow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:66:#     moved container, moved head arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:70:#   arrows from appearing between a source head and its own destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:76:# - The head arrow points the same way as the internal motif, acting as a second\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:81:# - Each assembly contains one container, one source arrow, one destination arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:83:#   head lands exactly on its destination arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:87:# - Orange growth is structurally tied to the same inferred direction: the arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:92:#   old same-side head as an arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:131:def _arrow_template(inner_h: int, inner_w: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:156:    base = _arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:185:        template = set(_arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:193:def _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h: int, outer_w: int, attach_side: str, anchor: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:203:def _stamp_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, tl: tuple[int, int], direction: str, color: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:233:    - Read direction from the internal orange arrow template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:234:    - The adjacent external 3x3 arrow is the movable head sprite, but its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:236:    - Move container + head toward the nearest matching arrow destination along\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:370:    for r, c in _arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:414:        head_r, head_c = _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h, outer_w, attach_side, anchor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:516:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (hr, hc), spec[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:517:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (dr, dc), spec[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/21/code.py:551:        _stamp_arrow(expected, (nhr, nhc), spec[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:289:    Recolor particles as they thread through a narrow corridor, using alternating turn priority with a backup turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:298:    - Because the path is a narrow corridor, the particle keeps moving straight until the corridor wall blocks its next cell; that blocked wall cell is marked with the end color if it is background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:323:    \"\"\"Reject local rooms so the path reads as a narrow 1-2 cell corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:348:    \"\"\"Build a single narrow serpentine corridor that guarantees an early fallback turn.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:388:    # At most one gentle width-2 bulge keeps the corridor visibly narrow instead of turning it into a room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/10/code.py:63:#    In the output the near group stays flat, the middle group becomes tall/narrow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:185:def _narrow_vertical_corridor(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:432:        if not _narrow_vertical_corridor(grid, jc, top1, jr, child_n, min_open_steps=5):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/29/code.py:435:        if not _narrow_vertical_corridor(grid, right_root[1], top2, jr, child_n, min_open_steps=6):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:34:#      target. If a choke narrows below 6, the mover stops at the farthest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:74:#    - Big mover sizes 5..7 make narrow gates visibly narrower than the mover.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:84:#      large mover footprint interacting with visibly narrow chokepoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:308:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, max(1, n - 2))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/18/code.py:309:    remove = int(n - narrow_w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/28/code.py:390:      generated tasks connector color already narrows the candidate set, and the final validation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_parent_retest_20260516.json:241:    \"name\": \"箭头标记反射方向 + 反射轴由锚块特征决定\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_parent_retest_20260516.json:335:    \"name\": \"显式分割线 + 连接器匹配 + 箭头标记反射\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_parent_review_summary_20260516.json:210:      \"name\": \"箭头标记反射方向 + 反射轴由锚块特征决定\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/c