 for color legend\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:32:#       the last gravity-reachable placement above the first too-narrow slice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:66:#       the last shaft becomes narrower row by row. In blocked examples the mover stops just above\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:67:#       the narrow segment while the red square remains below it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:77:#       gravity-like descent plus a monotone narrowing that eventually becomes too tight.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/2/code.py:226:      too narrow for the square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:226:    Original sliding-square physics on a very sparse narrow river, followed by a tight crop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:331:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/16/code.py:332:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/19/code.py:25:#   exercising the sequential-consumption rule beyond one narrow branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/9/code.py:409:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/9/code.py:410:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/4/code.py:39:      1) 同方向但错连接器，证明不能只看箭头；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/10/code.py:19:#      the farthest reachable placement before a chokepoint narrower than n.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db0c5428/37/code.py:416:    - The damaged corner cannot be located from \"blank space\" because the hole already contains plausible pixels. Opposite-corner symmetry narrows the answer to a pair, and the filled D5-style center supplies the extra anchor that reveals which corner needs repair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/20/code.py:165:    The answer is not found by global glyph identity. Color only narrows the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/31/code.py:16:#   output transform; it is a deliberately narrower, cleaner input family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/7/code.py:159:    - A narrow legend strip occupies the left edge. Each 3x3 legend glyph has one trigger color at its center plus a gray shape that specifies that color's ray behavior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:32:#      combo: detect arrow-shaped mover -> read its tip direction -> read border control\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:37:#    - n is restricted to 2..4. This keeps the arrow decomposition legible and avoids\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:57:#    - Across examples, humans can see one arrowed object, one plain target square, one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:58:#      red boundary dot, and outputs that sometimes follow the arrow and sometimes defy it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:103:def _arrow_square_info(comp: dict) -> dict | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:261:        mover_info = _arrow_square_info(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:404:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:405:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:793:    arrow_step = control_step if agree else (decoy_step if control_step == main_step else main_step)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:795:    tip = _choose_tip_cell(grid, mover_r, mover_c, n, STEP_TO_NAME[arrow_step])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/8/code.py:40:#    - The scatter freedom stays narrow: inter-band gaps are only 6 or 7, and within-band\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/24/code.py:44:#    - The new freedom is deliberately narrow. Irregularity is only 0/1 jitter on one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:47:  - a later horizontal gate may narrow to height 2, so it still passes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:48:  - the final horizontal gate may narrow to height 1, so the 2-high token stops\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:53:  - horizontal and vertical narrowings test different rectangle dimensions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:346:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:347:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/5/code.py:28:#        original task: the black square stops because the blue river narrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头源+标记配对+X形双线\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:17:#    - Combo task: each endpoint is replaced by a 3-cell blue L-arrow. The degree-2 corner is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:18:#      the tip, and the missing diagonal quadrant is the arrow's forward direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:19:#    - Each arrow tip has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker pixel in a non-blue,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:20:#      non-magenta color. Two arrows with the same marker color are one pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:21:#    - For one pair, the two tips lie on a common 45-degree diagonal and the arrows face each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:28:#      combo logic: blue arrows with tips at (2,2),(6,6), same red marker color, facing toward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:40:#    - Original blue-pixel grouping by diagonal is invalid: each arrow contains an incidental\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:43:#      colors attached to arrow tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:50:#      2. every arrow tip has exactly one adjacent non-bg, non-blue, non-magenta marker;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:51:#      3. every marker color labels exactly two arrows;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:52:#      4. paired arrows lie on one diagonal and face each other;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:57:#    - Both arrow bodies, both X branches, markers, triggers, and emitted rays must stay in-bounds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:68:#      1. blue L-shapes identify arrow tips and directions;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:69:#      2. repeated marker colors identify which distant arrows pair up;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:144:def _arrow_cells(tip: tuple[int, int], direction: tuple[int, int]) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:156:def _parse_arrow_component(comp: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:178:def _find_arrow_sources(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[dict]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:181:    arrows: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:199:            parsed = _parse_arrow_component(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:203:            arrows.append({\"tip\": tip, \"direction\": direction, \"cells\": comp})\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:205:    arrows.sort(key=lambda item: item[\"tip\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:206:    return arrows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:231:    assert dr != 0 and abs(dr) == abs(dc), \"paired arrow tips must share a diagonal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:238:    raise AssertionError(\"paired arrows must face each other along their tip diagonal\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:265:    arrows = _find_arrow_sources(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:267:    for arrow in arrows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:268:        tip = arrow[\"tip\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:277:        marker_groups.setdefault(markers[0], []).append(arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:376:    Read marked blue arrow pairs, expand each pair into an X, and emit magenta rays from triggers touched by either branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:379:    - The background is the most common color. Active blue objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows; the degree-2 corner is the tip and the missing diagonal quadrant gives the arrow's facing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:380:    - Each arrow tip has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker pixel in a non-blue, non-magenta color. Two arrows with the same marker color belong together.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:384:    - For every marker-matched arrow pair, use the two tips as the endpoints of a direct diagonal and verify that the arrows face each other along it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:389:    - The solution must combine three cues at once: arrow geometry tells you where the real endpoints are and which way they face, repeated marker colors tell you which two arrows form a pair, and each pair generates an entire X so triggers can activate from either branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:397:    arrows = _find_arrow_sources(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:398:    assert arrows, \"grid must contain at least one valid blue arrow source\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:401:    for arrow in arrows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:402:        tip = arrow[\"tip\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:411:        assert len(markers) == 1, \"each arrow tip must have exactly one adjacent marker\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:412:        marker_groups.setdefault(markers[0][2], []).append(arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:426:        assert len(group) == 2, \"each marker color must label exactly two arrows\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:517:        p_cells = _arrow_cells(p, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:518:        q_cells = _arrow_cells(q, (-dr, -dc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:519:        pair_arrow_cells = p_cells | q_cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:520:        if any(not (0 <= r < h and 0 <= c < w) for r, c in pair_arrow_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:522:        if any(cell in occupied or cell in drawn for cell in pair_arrow_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:527:        for cell in pair_arrow_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:558:        if any(cell in occupied or cell in drawn or cell in pair_arrow_cells for cell in ray_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:563:        pair_blue_cells = blue_occupied | pair_arrow_cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:564:        forbidden = occupied | drawn | path_cells | ray_cells | pair_arrow_cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:577:            \"arrow_cells\": (p_cells, q_cells),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:610:        p_cells, q_cells = pair[\"arrow_cells\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:632:        p_cells, q_cells = pair[\"arrow_cells\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/_final_summary_20260517.json:62:    \"name\": \"箭头源+标记配对\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/_final_summary_20260517.json:166:    \"name\": \"箭头源+标记配对+X形双线\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:33:#      combo task: one later spiral step is narrowed below width n, so the next spiral cell becomes infeasible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:46:#    - Width variation is limited to a few one-cell bulges and one optional narrowing gate. That is enough to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:62:#    - The narrowing gate only erases part of the leading row/column of the next spiral placement, preserving\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:67:#    - Reachable vs stuck examples differ by a visible local narrowing on a later ring or turn. The side bulge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:32:     real chokepoint narrower than n and the mover always halts upstream.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:75:  human to infer \"the river gets erased behind the sliding block until the first too-narrow gate.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:383:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:384:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头标记反射方向 + 反射轴由锚块特征决定\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:26:#   1. one green arrow glyph placed near the target anchor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:28:# - The arrow gives the mandatory \"primary\" reflection:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:29:#     right arrow  -> LR reflection is required,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:30:#     down arrow   -> UD reflection is required.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:32:#   also needed. Concretely, after reading the arrow, the solver compares the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:38:#     1. read the local arrow; if it is a down arrow, start from UD instead,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:42:#   Difference: quadrant position no longer selects the mirror; the arrow gives\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:46:# - The arrow vocabulary stays tiny: exactly two 3x3 glyphs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:49:#   arrows alone are insufficient, and anchors alone are ambiguous without first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:50:#   knowing which primary axis the arrow selected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:60:#   must remove arrow markers before stamping or they would leak into the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:62:#   arrows exist only outside TL, and the TL motif remains one 4-connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:66:# - The right arrow is drawn 1 cell above the anchor; the down arrow is drawn 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:71:# - The arrow is kept disconnected from the anchor, so component extraction for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:75:# - A human can read the arrow as the obvious first instruction, then notice\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:76:#   that two targets with the same arrow can still differ because of the anchor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:78:# - The generator enforces both arrow types, both anchor states, and at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:82:# - Green is reserved for arrows and never used inside the motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:84:#   anchor, while arrows sit outside with a one-cell gap. This avoids overlap and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:88:# - No hidden color ordering is used. Red still marks anchors, green means arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:91:#   \"arrows only\" or \"original quadrant rule\" at the whole-output level.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:95:# - Every non-TL quadrant has exactly one arrow glyph and exactly one decorated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:97:# - Each target anchor matches exactly one of two templates once its arrow-chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:212:def _read_arrow_primaries(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:225:        assert key != (0, 0), \"arrows are only allowed in non-TL quadrants\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:226:        assert key not in primaries, \"each non-TL quadrant must contain exactly one arrow glyph\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:229:            raise AssertionError(\"unrecognized arrow glyph\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:233:        assert key in primaries, \"each non-TL quadrant must contain exactly one arrow glyph\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:254:    Replicate the TL motif across quadrants with size scaling, arrow-selected primary reflection, and anchor-selected extra reflection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:259:    - Each non-TL quadrant contains one decorated red anchor plus exactly one nearby green arrow glyph; the anchor size still varies by quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:263:    - In each target quadrant, read the arrow first to get the mandatory reflection axis: right arrow means LR, down arrow means UD.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:264:    - Compare the observed target-anchor template against the TL anchor under either that primary flip alone or both flips; apply the matching transform to the full source motif, scale by anchor-size ratio, align the red region to the target anchor, and stamp non-background pixels. Remove the green arrows from the final output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:266:    Key insight: The arrow does not fully specify the transform by itself. It only chooses the primary axis; the anchor's internal asymmetry tells you whether an additional orthogonal flip must be composed on top of it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:275:    primaries, marker_components = _read_arrow_primaries(g, mid_r, mid_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:515:def _paint_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, top: int, left: int, shape: frozenset[tuple[int, int]]) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:520:def _place_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, anchor_r: int, anchor_c: int, primary: tuple[bool, bool]) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:523:        _paint_arrow(grid, anchor_r - 4, anchor_c, shape)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:525:        _paint_arrow(grid, anchor_r, anchor_c - 4, shape)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:611:    arrow_only_out = _build_output(patch, anchor_patch, tl_r0, tl_c0, target_sizes, anchors, primaries)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:613:    if int(np.count_nonzero(out != arrow_only_out)) < MIN_VARIANT_DIFF:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:624:        _place_arrow(inp, ar, ac, primaries[key])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/19/code.py:627:    # it is the reason arrow_only_out differs from out.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/7/code.py:59:#    - The legend is confined to a narrow corner strip with blank separator rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:518:    use_narrow_hint = (n == 1 and random.random() < 0.75) or (n >= 2 and not reached)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/34/code.py:617:    if use_narrow_hint and cut_idx is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:400:    use_narrow_hint = (n == 1 and random.random() < 0.75) or (n >= 2 and not reached)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:489:    if use_narrow_hint:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:523:        if use_narrow_hint and not geo_ok:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:525:        if not use_narrow_hint and geo_ok != dest_ok:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:71:#     The corridor/background inversion is inferable from large-area corners vs narrow strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:319:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/36/code.py:320:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/13/code.py:265:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/13/code.py:266:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:12:#   or at the farthest reachable interior placement before a narrow gate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:51:#   examples, it stops inside just before a narrow section. No overlapping markers or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:296:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:297:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/27/code.py:359:    \"\"\"Sample many near-sized areas from a narrow band.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:23:#   Walls isolate one narrow chamber, so a human can see the front maroon disappear first,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:293:    - Magenta walls form narrow corridors near the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/23/code.py:337:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/23/code.py:338:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/41/code.py:52:  - original blocker source: river narrows below width n,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:349:    - Each activated blob launches a ray from its uniquely narrowest extreme side, with width 1 or 2 from that side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头源+标记配对\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:18:#    - In this combo, each active source endpoint becomes a 3-cell blue L-arrow. The degree-2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:19:#      corner is the tip; the missing quadrant is the arrow's forward diagonal direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:20:#    - Each arrow also has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker cell in a non-blue,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:21:#      non-magenta color. Marker colors are the pairing labels: two arrows with the same marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:22:#      color form one active pair. The segment is drawn between their tips, and both arrows must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:24:#    - Example: suppose arrows A and B have red markers. A's tip is at (3,3) and points SE;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:26:#      inside the arrow bodies and could not tell which blue cells are endpoints. New logic first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:27:#      parses each 4-connected 3-cell L, extracts its tip/direction, groups arrows by marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:31:#      arrow distractor on the same diagonal extension as a real pair. Geometry-only pairing would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:40:#    - At most one uniquely marked distractor arrow is added. That is enough to make marker-based\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:44:#    - The old `by_color[line_color]` pool is invalid because a single arrow contains three blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:51:#      3-cell L arrow, each such arrow must have exactly one adjacent marker, active marker colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:52:#      must appear on exactly two arrows, and those two arrows must face each other along a shared\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:59:#      distractor arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:60:#    - Marker cells are attached to the tip side of an arrow, stay off all active diagonals and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:61:#      future rays, and touch only their own arrow in 4-neighborhood.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:63:#      arrow unambiguously.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:66:#    - Humans can directly see the L-arrow cue and infer that the diagonal leaves the tip through\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:68:#    - Repeated marker colors across distant arrows make the pairing label visible in a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:71:#      then connect arrow tips\" is more plausible than any accidental one-off geometry heuristic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:76:#    - Markers sit beside arrow tips instead of on the diagonal itself, so arrows, labels, path\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:78:#    - Distractor arrows, when present, are placed on diagonal extensions outside the active\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:82:#    - Marker colors do not transform into output colors; they only label which arrows belong\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:123:def _arrow_cells(tip: tuple[int, int], direction: tuple[int, int]) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:157:def _find_arrows(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> list[dict]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:160:    arrows: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:206:            assert len(marker_cells) == 1, \"each arrow must have exactly one adjacent marker\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:208:            arrows.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:218:    arrows.sort(key=lambda a: (a[\"tip\"], a[\"marker_color\"]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:219:    return arrows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:235:def _active_pairs_from_arrows(arrows: list[dict]) -> list[dict]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:237:    for arrow in arrows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:238:        marker_groups.setdefault(arrow[\"marker_color\"], []).append(arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:248:        assert ordered is not None, \"same-color arrow pair must be diagonal and face inward\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:265:    Read marked blue arrow sprites as diagonal endpoints, connect same-marked arrow pairs, then emit rays from magenta cells on those diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:268:    - bg = most common color. Blue source objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows whose corner cell is the tip and whose missing quadrant gives the forward diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:269:    - Each arrow has one orthogonally adjacent marker cell in a non-blue, non-magenta color. Marker colors that appear twice define the active arrow pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:270:    - Magenta trigger cells may lie on the interior of active diagonals; uniquely marked arrows or off-diagonal magenta cells can appear as distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:273:    - Parse every valid blue arrow, group arrows by marker color, and for each marker color that labels exactly two arrows, draw the blue diagonal segment between their tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:277:    - Neither raw blue geometry nor marker colors alone are sufficient: the L-shape identifies the true tip and diagonal direction, while the repeated marker color decides which two arrows should actually be connected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:285:    arrows = _find_arrows(grid, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:286:    assert arrows, \"grid must contain at least one valid blue arrow\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:289:    for pair in _active_pairs_from_arrows(arrows):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:403:    Ablation: parse arrows but ignore marker colors, pairing each arrow with its farthest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:410:    arrows = _find_arrows(grid, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:413:    arrows_by_tip = {arrow[\"tip\"]: arrow for arrow in arrows}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:415:    for arrow in arrows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:418:        for other in arrows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:419:            if other is arrow:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:421:            ordered = _ordered_pair(arrow, other)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:424:            dist = abs(other[\"tip\"][0] - arrow[\"tip\"][0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:429:            pair = tuple(sorted((arrow[\"tip\"], best_tip)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:434:        left = arrows_by_tip[p]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:435:        right = arrows_by_tip[q]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:490:        start_cells = _arrow_cells(start, start_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:491:        end_cells = _arrow_cells(end, end_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:492:        all_arrow_cells = start_cells | end_cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:495:        if any(not _in_bounds(h, w, cell) for cell in all_arrow_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:497:        if any(cell in occupied or cell in drawn for cell in all_arrow_cells | path_interior):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:499:        if any(cell in blue_occupied for cell in all_arrow_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:501:        if any(nbr in blue_occupied for cell in all_arrow_cells for nbr in _neighbors4(*cell)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:509:            \"arrows\": [\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:540:def _try_place_decoy_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:566:        cells = _arrow_cells(tip, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:620:        temp_blue = blue_occupied | placed[\"arrows\"][0][\"cells\"] | placed[\"arrows\"][1][\"cells\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:621:        for arrow in placed[\"arrows\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:622:            marker_cell = _find_marker_cell(arrow[\"tip\"], arrow[\"direction\"], h, w, temp_occupied, drawn | ray_cells | future_drawn, temp_blue)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:636:        for arrow in placed[\"arrows\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:637:            occupied.update(arrow[\"cells\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:638:            blue_occupied.update(arrow[\"cells\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:656:        placed = _try_place_decoy_arrow(segment, h, w, occupied, blue_occupied, drawn)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:676:        for arrow, marker_cell in zip(seg[\"arrows\"], seg[\"marker_cells\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:677:            for r, c in arrow[\"cells\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:697:            if any(abs(r - arrow[\"tip\"][0]) + abs(c - arrow[\"tip\"][1]) == 1 for seg in segments for arrow in seg[\"arrows\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:164:        raise AssertionError(\"vertical cross must have one uniquely narrow end arm\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:183:    raise AssertionError(\"horizontal cross must have one uniquely narrow end arm\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:188:    Build a red ray network by activating single-axis cross blobs whose narrowest arm is a hidden port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:196:    - The activated cross then emits a ray from the uniquely narrowest arm tip, with width 1 or 2 depending on that arm.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:199:    Key insight: Direction is encoded geometrically, not by color. The only arm end that is strictly narrower than the other three extremes is the implicit launch port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:334:# - a constant narrow top arm (width 1 or 2),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/33/code.py:248:    - A unique red cell marks the middle of a green 3x3 destination block, while maroon pixels sit on narrow floor corridors or in isolated pockets outside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/29/code.py:190:      narrow arm tip. One marker ray may already be fully pre-expanded as an example.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/21/code.py:38:# - 不增加文字、箭头或标记层；对象仍是标准 ARC 块状轮廓。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/30/code.py:26:#    The fusion matters because D12 narrows the motif space to a recognizable typed vocabulary, while D3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/30/code.py:28:  colors, so color only narrows the search to a group; it does not identify the true `dst`\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1ae2feb7/3/code.py:292:        raise ValueError(\"bar side too narrow for sampled separator gap\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头精灵大瓦片颜色循环\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:18:#    - Anchor cue: the big monochrome objects are now rotated arrow sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:25:#    Example: if a right-pointing arrow carries a 3x2 seed on its lower flank,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:30:#    The variant would become ambiguous if arrow directions, seed sizes, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:33:#    - one arrow template family,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:37:#    Seeds still differ by internal texture and arrow orientation, so the combo\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:42:#      clockwise flank, orthogonal to the ray. We must recognize arrow shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:45:#      origin from the matched arrow geometry plus a globally inferred tile size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:50:#      color by exact arrow-shape matches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:53:#    The generator is output-first. It places arrows with one-cell guard bands,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:55:#    any previous non-background payload. This guarantees that each arrow has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:56:#    exactly one adjacent non-arrow component and label-based extraction stays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:61:#    shows all three cues: the arrow points one way while the seed sits on a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:63:#    the same geometry but cycle their colors. Other arrows reuse the same size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:68:#    other, and each grid uses only 2-4 arrows. This prevents component merges\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:79:#    - every sample uses at least two arrow orientations,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:85:#    - All arrows share one of the known templates, up to rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:87:#    - Exactly one adjacent marker component per arrow is present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:196:def _oriented_arrow_spec(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:206:def _match_arrow_component(mask: np.ndarray) -> dict | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:210:            rotated, launch_local, attach_normal = _oriented_arrow_spec(spec, direction_name)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:221:def _detect_arrow_color(grid: np.ndarray, *, bg: int) -> int | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:235:            if _match_arrow_component(local) is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:399:    Extend large marker tiles from arrow anchors, cycling colors on every repeated chunk.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:403:    - One non-background color forms several rotated arrow sprites from a small fixed template family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:404:    - Each arrow has exactly one adjacent large rectangular seed marker on a side flank, and exactly one arrow in the grid keeps its full long ray as the clue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:407:    - Read each arrow's pointing direction from its silhouette rather than from the marker attachment side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:408:    - Infer the shared seed-tile size from the compact markers, reconstruct the clue arrow's first tile, and learn a global color permutation by comparing consecutive full chunks on the long clue ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:409:    - For every arrow, repeat its seed rectangle outward in the arrow direction until the boundary, applying one more step of the learned color cycle after each whole-tile advance; arrow pixels are never overwritten.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:412:    The task now fuses three cues: arrow shape gives direction, the payload is a large textured rectangle, and the single long example ray reveals that repetition preserves geometry but rotates colors through a fixed global cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:419:    arrow_color = _detect_arrow_color(g, bg=int(bg))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:420:    if arrow_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:423:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_color), connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:424:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:428:    arrow_records: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:431:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:432:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:433:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:436:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:437:        local_arrow = g[int(ar0) : int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0) : int(ac1) + 1] == int(arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:438:        matched = _match_arrow_component(local_arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:443:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:467:        arrow_records.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:475:    if not arrow_records:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:484:    for record in arrow_records:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:501:        if np.any(tile == int(bg)) or np.any(tile == int(arrow_color)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:527:            protect={int(arrow_color)},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:680:def _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:691:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:694:    arrow_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:699:    patch, launch_local, attach_normal = _oriented_arrow_spec(spec, direction_name)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:711:        arrow_cells = _component_cells(patch, (r0, c0))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:712:        if not _cells_clear(arrow_cells, occ, arrow_guard, payload_guard):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:727:        if not _cells_clear(payload_cells, occ, arrow_guard, payload_guard):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:730:        for r, c in arrow_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:732:            out[int(r), int(c)] = int(arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:733:        _mark_guard(arrow_guard, arrow_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:758:    arrows: list[dict],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:762:    keep_idx = next(i for i, meta in enumerate(arrows) if bool(meta[\"is_clue\"]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:763:    for i, meta in enumerate(arrows):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:789:    arrow_color = _detect_arrow_color(g, bg=int(bg))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:790:    if arrow_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:793:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_color), connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:794:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:800:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:801:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:802:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:804:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:805:        local_arrow = g[int(ar0) : int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0) : int(ac1) + 1] == int(arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:806:        matched = _match_arrow_component(local_arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:810:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:861:            protect={int(arrow_color)},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:874:    arrow_color = int(rng.choice(others))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:875:    cycle_colors = list(map(int, rng.choice([c for c in others if int(c) != int(arrow_color)], size=_CYCLE_LEN, replace=False)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:891:    arrow_guard = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:894:    arrows: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:896:        meta = _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:907:            arrow_guard=arrow_guard,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:910:            arrow_color=int(arrow_color),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:915:        arrows.append(meta)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:917:    inp = _build_input_from_output(out, arrows, int(bg))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:77:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(-2, 0)], \"flanks\": [(-2, -1), (-2, 1)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:85:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(-4, 0)], \"flanks\": [(-4, -1), (-4, 1)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:97:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(0, 2)], \"flanks\": [(-1, 2), (1, 2)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:105:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(0, 4)], \"flanks\": [(-1, 4), (1, 4)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:117:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(2, 0)], \"flanks\": [(2, -1), (2, 1)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:125:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(4, 0)], \"flanks\": [(4, -1), (4, 1)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:137:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(0, -2)], \"flanks\": [(-1, -2), (1, -2)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:145:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(0, -4)], \"flanks\": [(-1, -4), (1, -4)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:51:#    Yellow and teal are confined to narrow corridors outside the destination. Teal overrides yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:218:    - The fill order is still controlled by reachability and distance, but the fused variant exposes two nested BFS products: the full reachable background region and the narrower subset of floor cells that lie on the transport routes of the collected maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:30:#    This makes the combo visually distinct from the original narrow markers without\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:5:# Name: 螺旋射线+箭头形起始标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:20:#    - New start object: a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite. Four red body pixels make the shaft/wedge and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:21:#      one yellow pixel protrudes on the firing side. The arrow tail is anchored on the boundary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:29:#    - Example sketch: if a right-pointing arrow starts near the left edge, the first leg goes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:35:#    - Direction freedom is limited to the four cardinals and one arrow family, so the start cue is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:44:#      above it. That is false now, so start detection must match the arrow geometry instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:51:#    - New solver assumption: exactly one arrow exists; its red body has area 4; it has exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:55:#    - Objects are still placed output-first. The generator paints the arrow, then for each active\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:62:#    - The arrow makes the initial direction visible without reading color ids. Horizontal starts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:76:#      \"read direction from the arrow, then follow repeated clockwise turns.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:95:# --- Start arrow ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:579:    Build a red activation network whose first launch comes from a small arrow and whose rays curl clockwise into spirals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:584:    - The start marker is no longer a bottom stem; it is a boundary-anchored red arrow sprite with one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:588:    - Recolor the whole start arrow red, then launch a ray from the yellow tip in the direction implied\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:589:      by the arrow shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:597:    - Two cues must be read together: the arrow geometry gives the initial direction, and the repeated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:604:    # --- STEP 1) Detect the start arrow sprite and infer the initial direction ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:694:    # --- STEP 5) Trace the arrow-launched spiral until it hits a blob or exhausts itself ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:732:    # Place the directional start arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:28:#    a single memorized picture, but the family stays narrow enough to remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/21/code.py:50:#    narrower and top-cropped relative to the input. A human can therefore infer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/24/code.py:43:#    The design is intentionally narrow instead of fully free-form:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/45/code.py:22:#     arm_len: generator keeps equal cardinal arms, but narrows the visible regime to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/45/code.py:344:# The generator intentionally narrows the arm/size regime to compact boards where\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:14:#     - After solving on the full canvas, the output is cropped to the narrow strip containing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:128:    - After reconstructing the full solved canvas, keep only the narrow strip that contains the crosshairs and solved sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/23/code.py:61:    Detect embedded '+' motifs inside a narrow strip and recolor each one to teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/23/code.py:66:    - The true '+' motifs are arranged on one shared row or one shared column, so they read as a narrow 1-D chain, while other foreground cells are only distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:203:    - Magenta walls carve the board into a narrow maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/26/code.py:82:#   - Human solvers can compare narrow vs wide frames and see that one dot centers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/37/code.py:42:#    is visible in the output as wider or narrower rectangular corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7666fa5d/8/code.py:38:     by earlier, narrower stages.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/16/code.py:26:#          carve long narrow chambers rather than roughly square rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:36:#      component, orthogonal rooms, and a small number of narrow chokepoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:48:#      narrow doorway would be mistaken for a real passage and the maze would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:41:  The fused rule instead gives the narrow upper red frame two dots at its legal width-7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:44:  frame color narrows candidates, spatial proximity resolves shared colors, and frame width\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/24/code.py:92:  differs between narrow and wide frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/31/code.py:37:#      usually horizontal only: blank outer columns disappear, producing a narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/31/code.py:50:#    - To keep the change legible, generator columns come from two narrow but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头形精灵凸出方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:15:# - This combo replaces the source object with arrow-shaped anchors and simultaneously changes the direction cue:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:16:#   the ray must follow the arrow's protruding head, not the side where the seed happens to touch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:18:#   Example: a right-facing arrow may have its seed above or below it, but the output still repeats that seed to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:24:# - Each grid uses at least two arrow orientations, so the shape cue is actually demonstrated inside one sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:26:# - `detect_dominant_big_component_color()` still works because arrows remain the only components with bbox >= 3x3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:31:# - The generator is output-first: place full arrows and full rays first, then erase all but one long clue ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:32:# - Arrows, rays, and their 4-neighborhood guards are kept separate so two non-arrow components never merge under\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:33:#   `label_mask((grid != bg) & (grid != arrow_color))`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:34:# - Candidate seeds are rejected if they go out of bounds, overlap, or even touch previously committed rays / arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:36:# - The crucial cue is human-visible geometry: each arrow has one protruding tip and that tip points the repetition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:38:# - The kept pre-extended clue ray shows that the repeated payload follows the arrow orientation rather than contact.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:41:# - No ray is allowed to touch a foreign arrow or another ray, so each object stays visually isolated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:44:# - No ordering on color ids is used. Colors only separate background / arrow anchors / payload tiles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:47:# - For every generated arrow, the attachment side should be orthogonal to the true ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:50:# - Solver assumes each big anchor component exactly matches one rotated arrow template below.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:51:# - Solver assumes each arrow has exactly one adjacent non-arrow component (seed or pre-extended ray component).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:215:def _build_arrow_lookup() -> dict[tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:224:_ARROW_LOOKUP = _build_arrow_lookup()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:227:def _match_arrow_direction(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:254:def detect_arrow_component_color(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:260:    \"\"\"Choose the color whose big components best match the arrow template family.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:283:            if _match_arrow_direction(local) is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:295:# Extend marker rays from arrow-shaped anchors using the arrow head as the only direction cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:298:# - One dominant non-background color forms several arrow sprites, all drawn from the same small template family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:299:# - Each arrow touches exactly one colored marker component, and exactly one of those components may already be a long\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:302:# - Recognize the arrow's facing direction from its protruding tip, not from the marker's contact side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:304:# - Repeat that tile from its current seed position all the way to the boundary in the arrow-indicated direction,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:305:#   while preserving arrow-colored cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:308:#   fails. Only the arrow silhouette's asymmetric protrusion consistently identifies the ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:315:    arrow_col = detect_arrow_component_color(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:316:    if arrow_col is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:319:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_col), connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:320:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_col))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:324:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:325:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:326:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:329:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:330:        local_arrow = arrow_mask[int(ar0):int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0):int(ac1) + 1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:331:        direction = _match_arrow_direction(local_arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:336:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:362:            protect={int(arrow_col)},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:543:def _cells_clear_for_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:546:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:550:        if int(occ[r, c]) != 0 or bool(arrow_guard[r, c]) or bool(ray_guard[r, c]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:558:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:560:    own_arrow: set[tuple[int, int]],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:563:        if (int(r), int(c)) in own_arrow:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:567:        if bool(arrow_guard[r, c]) or bool(ray_guard[r, c]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:572:def _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:580:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:583:    arrow_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:593:        arrow_cells = _component_cells(patch, (r0, c0))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:594:        if not _cells_clear_for_arrow(arrow_cells, occ, arrow_guard, ray_guard):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:612:            own_arrow = set((int(r), int(c)) for r, c in arrow_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:613:            if not _cells_clear_for_ray(ray_cells, occ, arrow_guard, ray_guard, own_arrow):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:616:            for rr, cc in arrow_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:618:                out[rr, cc] = int(arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:619:            _mark_guard(arrow_guard, arrow_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:641:    arrows: list[dict],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:645:    pre_idx = max(range(len(arrows)), key=lambda i: arrows[i][\"tiles\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:646:    if arrows[pre_idx][\"tiles\"] < _PRE_EXT_IDEAL_TILES:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:647:        candidates = [i for i, meta in enumerate(arrows) if meta[\"tiles\"] >= _PRE_EXT_IDEAL_TILES]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:652:    for i, meta in enumerate(arrows):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:666:        raise ValueError(f\"unsupported arrow count: {n}\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:691:    arrow_color = int(rng.choice(others))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:692:    palette = [c for c in others if c != arrow_color]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:700:    arrow_guard = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:703:    arrows: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:705:        meta = _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:713:            arrow_guard,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:716:            arrow_color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:720:        arrows.append(meta)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:722:    inp = _build_input_from_output(out, arrows, bg, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/17/code.py:31:#   and the cropped fill stays in a narrow range, making the edge-stop + tight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/18/code.py:27:#        narrowed interval, stop before painting the stripe;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/18/code.py:30:#      - gap line: if the original input has foreground inside the current narrowed interval,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/3/code.py:9:#   inside the original segment span. Originally, yellow stripes are narrow span-only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/3/code.py:10:#   marks, while green stripes are narrow but also flood the full row/column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/3/code.py:191:    - yellow stripes keep the original narrow segment span but flood the full row/col\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:28:#    The family is kept narrow on purpose: a vertical backbone crosses two horizontal lines, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头编码方向+标记修正方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:46:#    replaces that with one yellow edge-L arrow plus one colored corner marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:47:#    The arrow has two perpendicular arms that already encode an ordered pair of candidate\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:48:#    directions: the longer arm is the arrow's direct direction, and the shorter arm is exactly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:49:#    the clockwise-rotated alternative. Example: a top-edge arrow with elbow at (0, 6), long\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:55:#    on row 0 and later stripes appear on rows 2, 4, ... . The source arrow therefore matters\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:59:#    visible lengths and the longer arm is forced to be unique. That keeps the \"arrow points by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:68:#      direction. Now the edge only says \"the arrow is on this side\"; the actual direction comes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:73:#    - exactly one salient yellow component is the arrow source\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:79:#    The generator chooses one of eight edge templates so the arrow fits fully in-bounds, keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:81:#    corner marker only after the arrow is fixed. Interior blobs are placed with padded free\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:82:#    placement on a canvas that already contains the arrow and marker, so blobs cannot overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:86:#    starting source is now visibly an arrow-like L rather than a plain segment. Comparing a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:88:#    arrow's long arm or its clockwise-rotated shorter arm. Because the two candidate outputs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:92:#    `main()` assumes `_extract_arrow()` finds a single largest yellow L and that its shorter arm\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:98:#    contiguous row-span or col-span; the generator's arrow is made from straight runs, so that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:145:def _extract_arrow(g: np.ndarray) -> dict[str, object] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:202:    arrow: dict[str, object],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:208:    elbow_r, elbow_c = (int(v) for v in arrow[\"elbow\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:211:        move_dir = str(arrow[\"rot_dir\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:212:        span_arm = list(arrow[\"base_arm\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:214:        move_dir = str(arrow[\"base_dir\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:215:        span_arm = list(arrow[\"rot_arm\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:283:    arrow = _extract_arrow(g)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:284:    if arrow is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:286:    return _paint_pattern(g, bg, _layout(arrow, g.shape, rotated=rotated))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/11/code.py:291:    Propagate the original Y,Y,G stripe process, but decode direction from a yellow edge-L arrow\n/home/lixin