= out[r, c] = int(arrow1_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/16/code.py:513:    for r, c in permeable[\"arrow\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/16/code.py:514:        grid[r, c] = out[r, c] = int(arrow2_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:11:#      * 第一层是箭头中心（4/5 号）+ 同色对角装饰，表示“如果只看默认方向，应当按哪个转接槽方向转”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:16:#          blue(1) = 直行穿过，忽略箭头默认转向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:17:#          red(2)  = 执行箭头给出的转向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:19:#      若 c 处是红标记，则自上而下的信号会在箭头中心右转进入水平槽，原本在水平槽上的信号会向下落到该列；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:20:#      若 c 处是蓝标记，则即使中心箭头看起来在提示右转，垂直信号仍保持向下，水平信号仍保持向右。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:21:#      因而“箭头提供默认 turn family，颜色决定是否真的执行这次 turn”，蓝色就是显式的优先级覆盖案例。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:24:#    - 箭头家族只保留两类（左右交换槽），交叉颜色也只保留两类（直行 / 转弯），总离散档位很少，便于从 2-4 个样例归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:26:#      最终端点配对，否则这题就退化成“只读箭头”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:27:#    - token 颜色池避开箭头颜色 4/5，只与 red/blue 有轻度复用；这种复用通过结构区分：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:31:#    - 原 _trace_wire 依赖“交叉处直行优先”即可正确；在本变体里，纯箭头交叉和红色交叉都可能要求立刻离开当前方向，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:32:#      因此必须先识别箭头中心，再看是否有红/蓝覆盖。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:33:#    - 原 track_mask = 非背景减 token，会把箭头对角装饰误当轨道支路。新版只把 8/9、红蓝交叉夹子和“解码出的箭头中心”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:37:#    - 原 9-rect 识别只把 (5,8) 当作管道邻接。新版必须把 1/2/4/5 都视为 wire-like，否则矩形贴着箭头或交叉时会漏掉面连接。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:41:#    - 箭头对角装饰在同一方向家族内允许放在上侧或下侧；生成器按“上侧优先，否则下侧”的方式放置，避免相邻 crossover row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:43:#    - color-9 矩形只允许覆盖 0/8，不允许吞掉箭头中心、红蓝夹子或对角装饰，否则人类无法恢复两层路由线索。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:47:#    - 观察者可以同时看到：交叉中心出现彩色箭头、两侧再出现红/蓝成对夹子。相同箭头家族在多个交叉重复出现，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:48:#      但红蓝会把这些交叉分成“执行箭头转向”和“无视箭头直行”两类。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:49:#    - 当同一条水平槽上同时有红和蓝时，输出里的 token 排列会显示：有些列真的交换了信号，有些列虽然也有箭头却没有交换。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:50:#      这正是“颜色优先覆盖默认箭头”的可视证据。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:53:#    - 主线仍保持 8/9 的大块结构；箭头只占交叉中心和一个对角像素，红蓝标记只占中心左右两格，没有额外铺满局部区域。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:54:#    - token、箭头、交叉夹子、9-rect 各自的几何角色固定，视觉上容易分层：3x3 token、正交主线、矩形块、交叉提示。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:57:#    - 颜色变化只承担两类局部语义：4/5 是箭头方向家族，1/2 是“是否执行该箭头”的控制位。不存在隐藏的颜色算术或排序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:58:#    - 蓝色交叉是关键：它与红色交叉共享同类箭头，但输出行为不同，因此解题者能从少量样例学到优先级而不是把箭头当唯一规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:61:#    - solver 假设每个箭头中心都带有同家族的单个对角装饰，generator 的 _place_arrow_marker() 保证这一点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:62:#    - solver 假设每个带红蓝夹子的交叉一定也是一个已解码箭头中心；generator 在每个被彩色控制的交叉上总是先放箭头再放夹子。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:66:#    - 生成器额外计算“arrow-only 路由”和“融合规则路由”的底部落点差异；若二者完全一致，则说明蓝色覆盖没有实际生效，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:176:def _find_arrow_markers(g: np.ndarray) -> dict[tuple[int, int], int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:177:    \"\"\"Return {center: hdir} for decoded arrow-family junction markers.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:203:    arrow_markers: dict[tuple[int, int], int],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:205:    \"\"\"Return {arrow_center: PASS_MARK|TURN_MARK} for controlled interior crossings.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:209:    for r, c in arrow_markers:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:243:def _turn_dir_at_arrow(d: tuple[int, int], hdir: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:268:    arrow_markers: dict[tuple[int, int], int],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:272:    Follow one wire component using arrow-family defaults, red/blue overrides, and 9-rect pass-through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:274:    Pure arrow junctions always apply their turn family. At interior crossings, blue keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:275:    current direction while red executes that same arrow-family turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:282:            raise AssertionError(\"wire trace looped under arrow+color routing\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:309:        arrow_hdir = arrow_markers.get(cur)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:310:        if arrow_hdir is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:314:                nd = _turn_dir_at_arrow(d, arrow_hdir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:351:    Route colored 3x3 tokens through pipe networks whose default turns come from arrow junctions, but whose crossings can overrule those arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:356:    - Some junction centers are colored arrow markers (4/5) with a matching diagonal decoration; some of those same junctions also carry blue/red side markers that control the crossing behavior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:361:    - At an arrow-only junction, the signal follows the arrow's turn family. At an arrow+color crossing, red executes that turn while blue forces straight-through motion instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:365:    - The new challenge is two-layer routing: arrows define the default local turn map, but blue crossings visibly override that default. Correct endpoint pairing therefore depends on learning both the arrow family and the color priority.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:373:    arrow_markers = _find_arrow_markers(g)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:379:    for p in arrow_markers:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:392:    crossing_controls = _find_crossing_controls(track_mask, g, arrow_markers)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:426:                    end, dd = _trace_wire(comp, ep, (-odr, -odc), h, w, rects_9, arrow_markers, crossing_controls)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:435:                    end, dd = _trace_wire(comp, ep, (-odr, -odc), h, w, rects_9, arrow_markers, crossing_controls)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:506:def _place_arrow_marker(grid: np.ndarray, r: int, c: int, hdir: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:570:    Draw continuous channel columns plus arrow-marked row transfers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:572:    Each interior crossing gets both an arrow-family center and a red/blue control pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:573:    Blue keeps straight; red executes the arrow family's swap turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:595:        if not _place_arrow_marker(grid, xrow, src_col, hdir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:596:            raise AssertionError(\"failed to place source arrow marker\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:597:        if not _place_arrow_marker(grid, xrow, dst_col, hdir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:598:            raise AssertionError(\"failed to place destination arrow marker\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:610:            if not _place_arrow_marker(grid, xrow, c, hdir):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:611:                raise AssertionError(\"failed to place interior arrow marker\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:642:    \"\"\"Attempt to place one color-9 rectangle without swallowing arrow/color controls.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:818:    arrow_only_bottom = _bottom_slots(_simulate_rows(n, row_specs, force_all_turn=True))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:819:    priority_effect = sum(int(a != b) for a, b in zip(actual_bottom, arrow_only_bottom))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:861:    \"\"\"Helper for diagnostics of the fused arrow+crossing-control behavior.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头直线贯穿射线\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:23:#    - D3/0: the external source object becomes an arrow sprite with one ring tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:27:#    Example: an arrow touching the top ring at column c points downward into the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:29:#    entire interior column from top to bottom. If the arrow is two-colored, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:31:#    it. A bottom-touching arrow at the same column would paint the same geometry\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:37:#    - there are 2-3 arrows per grid, not just one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:38:#    - arrows can start from either of two opposite sides of the chosen axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:39:#    - monochrome and two-color arrows both appear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:40:#    - at least one arrow per sample is two-color so direction is behaviorally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:43:#    either vertical rays (top/bottom arrows) or horizontal rays (left/right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:44:#    arrows). That avoids row/column crossings that would otherwise create noisy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:49:#    - useful components no longer have >=2 ring touches; each arrow has exactly 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:52:#    - U-pairs are incompatible with \"one arrow -> one through-line\", so they are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:55:#    has the local arrow-head geometry for that side, then derives the full line\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:60:#    then converts each line into a single external arrow with:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:71:#    plainly an inward-pointing arrow attached to one side of the frame. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:82:#    Colors are structural, not id-based. Monochrome arrows produce solid rays.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:83:#    Two-color arrows alternate along the shaft and continue that alternation in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:90:#    component has one touch plus an arrow head, and the output is full-span\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:96:#    - that ring cell belongs to a valid arrow-head pattern for one side\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:98:#    - useful arrows do not intersect in the cropped output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:100:#    per sample, dedicated palette colors, and explicit arrow-shape validation in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:208:def _has_arrow_tip(coords: set[tuple[int, int]], tip: tuple[int, int], side: str) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:298:def _place_arrow_component(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:327:    Reconstruct full-span interior rays from external arrows around a framed rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:331:    - Useful external components are inward-pointing arrows. Each arrow has exactly one tip cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:336:    - Map each arrow tip to the corresponding interior boundary cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:339:    - Monochrome arrows paint solid rays; two-color arrows alternate starting from the tip color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:342:    - The arrow no longer encodes two endpoints. Its single ring tip fixes the line position, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:343:      the side/orientation of the arrow determines which full-span straight ray must be drawn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:382:        if side is None or not _has_arrow_tip(coords, tip, side):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:457:    Every sample contains at least one monochrome arrow and one two-color arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:467:def _arrow_specs(side: str, idx: int, H: int, W: int, r0: int, c0: int, r1: int, c1: int):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:586:        inner, backbone, head = _arrow_specs(side, idx, H, W, r0, c0, r1, c1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:600:        if not _place_arrow_component(grid, comp_mask, backbone, head, colors, bg):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/25/code.py:29:# - The variant is intentionally narrow rather than fully free-form:\n/home/lixinyu