alt_touch in wall_set or alt_touch in arrow_set:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/30/code.py:396:            if any(cell in occupied or cell in ray_set or cell in arrow_set or cell in wall_set for cell in final_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/30/code.py:402:            new_cells = set(arrow_pts) | ray_set | wall_set\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/30/code.py:403:            expected_count = len(arrow_pts) + len(ray_set) + len(wall_set)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/30/code.py:407:            for r, c in arrow_pts:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/30/code.py:416:                    \"arrow_pts\": arrow_pts,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:16:#     - Keep the original objects: 3-cell L arrows and 1/3-pixel axis-aligned walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:17:#     - Change 1 (D8): arrows do not fire independently. Sort them by squared distance from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:18:#       the ray source (the arrow's right-angle vertex) to the grid center, nearest first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:23:#     - Example: arrow A near the center goes first, side-bounces off a teal wall at (7,8),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:30:#     - Use exactly 2 arrows so the order cue is legible and the human can compare “near center”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:32:#     - Force one static-wall bounce on the center-near arrow so wall erasure is always visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:33:#     - Force one later trail collision on the farther arrow so the first-come-first-served rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:37:#     - Original `for start_col, pts in arrows:` assumed cross-arrow independence. This is invalid;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:38:#       solver must sort arrows by center distance before tracing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:52:#     - Generator plans the near-center arrow output-first: one bounce, one wall, then an exit\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:53:#       segment. Its arrow cells, wall pixels, and full output trail are all disjoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:54:#     - Generator then back-solves a second arrow whose straight path would next enter one chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:55:#       cell from the first trail. The second arrow stops there, so its own painted cells remain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:57:#     - The second arrow is constrained to be lexicographically earlier than the first source but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:61:#     - Across examples, input shows a near-center arrow plus a farther arrow. Output shows a wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:62:#       gap on the near-center arrow's bounce and a truncated far-arrow tail near the first trail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:63:#     - Because the farther arrow is often visually earlier on the page, humans can infer that the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:69:#     - Wall color differs from arrow colors so the post-bounce color change is structurally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:72:#     - Solver assumes arrow source distances are orderable; generator rejects center-distance ties.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:74:#       arrow away from the mandatory wall region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:76:#       makes the second arrow approach a chosen trail cell directly and avoids other wall adjacencies.\n/hom