code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:26:#    - Only two opening sizes are used: 2 -> narrow, 3 -> wide. This is enough to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:50:#      and often mixes narrow + wide openings in the same grid for contrast.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:695:    narrow_idx: int | None = None\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:696:    narrow_candidates = [i for i, available in enumerate(available_per_block) if i != wide_idx and 2 in available]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:697:    if block_count >= 2 and narrow_candidates and rng.random() < 0.8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:698:        narrow_idx = narrow_candidates[int(rng.integers(len(narrow_candidates)))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:704:        elif i == narrow_idx:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:704:def _place_docked_trains(base, bg, regions, arrow_color):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:725:            output[r0 + ir, c0 + ic] = arrow_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:740:def _scatter_trains(base, bg, regions, trains, arrow_color):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:750:        input_grid[ir, ic] = arrow_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:793:    arrow_candidates = [c for c in range(8) if c != bg and c not in stripe_colors]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:794:    if not arrow_candidates:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:796:    arrow_color = random.choice(arrow_candidates)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:798:    placed = _place_docked_trains(base, bg, regions, arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:803:    input_grid = _scatter_trains(base, bg, regions, trains, arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/3/code.py:10:#    with two couplers could only map to one size-2 station. Here the same train first narrows to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/3/code.py:78:    Key insight: coupler count is no longer sufficient by itself; it only narrows the search, and the region-stripe palette carried on the train resolves which equal-sized station is the true dock.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D9/1/code.py:70:# - Human-visible difference from the original task is strong: outputs are narrow cropped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D16/2/code.py:56:#        narrow slit -> dense beam\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:33:#     - 这个变体改为：方向只由容器内部的橙色箭头模板决定\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:36:#       具体选左/右或上/下必须看内部箭头\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:38:#     - mover 容器内部至少 3x3，初始橙色永远是一个 4-cell 箭头：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:44:#     - 容器只朝箭头指向的一侧移动；另一侧目标线是显式 decoy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:48:#     - solver 必须先读出内部箭头，例如 right，再只取右侧候选线，随后\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:51:#     - 没把方向做成任意图案，而是固定 4 种箭头模板，复杂度与 ARC 训练样例可观察性匹配\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:58:#       模板推方向，因此 grey-fill 排序也要改成“按箭头所指边 inward”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:69:#     - 箭头模板固定且醒目，2-3 个样例足以归纳“箭头朝哪边就往哪边走”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:74:#     - mover 的 interior orange 恰好等于 1 个箭头模板，因此方向检测唯一\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:93:def _arrow_template(inner_h: int, inner_w: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:118:    base = _arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:147:        tpl = set(_arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D1/2/code.py:288:    for r, c in _arrow_template(inner_h, inner_w, direction):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/0/code.py:67:      and at least two palette entries. The generator narrows size ranges and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D13/2/code.py:25:#    - The solver still supports all original collision branches. The generator narrows the placement space to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D8/1/code.py:40:#    Regions are 13x8, 13x8, 13x9 in each row. The source motif is kept narrow so its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D8/1/code.py:41:#    largest 2x scale fits inside the narrowest region. Anchor placement prefers positions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D8/1/code.py:294:    \"\"\"Build the source motif patch inside the narrow top-left region.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:3:# Change: 无符号编码（颜色匹配规则由示例隐含给出）... → 精灵内部的方向箭头标记\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:13:     an explicit 3-pixel arrow inside each source sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:15:     Sources replace the single interior pixel with a 3-pixel arrowhead made from the transfer color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:18:       new: source.arrow points right, exactly one destination lies to the right of that source ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:19:            copy source.arrow color into that destination center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:20:     The path still tells us which two sprites are destinations; the arrow only decides source->target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:23:   - The arrow alphabet is limited to four global directions: up/down/left/right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:24:   - Each sample contains exactly two arrow-bearing sources so the symbol is repeated and decodable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:33:     The arrow therefore uses only the center and corners, leaving cardinal border cells untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:43:     by the grey path, while the deleted source sprites visibly contain arrowheads that point toward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:46:     solver to use the arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:49:   - Only box sprites are used in this variant. That keeps the arrow symbols readable and avoids\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:55:   - The color transferred to a destination is simply the arrow color shown inside the matching source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:59:   - Assumption: every arrow source is a full 3x3 box with one of four known 3-pixel patterns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:136:    Source sprites have a 3-pixel inner arrow pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:192:def _decode_arrow(sprite: dict) -> str | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:193:    \"\"\"Return the arrow direction for a full 3x3 source sprite, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:220:    Transfer source arrow colors into the two path-connected bordered sprites, keeping only those destinations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:225:    - Non-destination boxes are either plain distractors or full 3x3 source boxes whose interior 3-pixel arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:230:    - For every arrow-bearing source sprite, decode its pointing direction and identify which destination lies in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:231:      that direction from the source. Copy the source arrow color into that destination center pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:297:        direction = _decode_arrow(sp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:301:        assert len(cands) == 1, \"each source arrow should identify exactly one destination\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:336:def _make_arrow_patch(border_color: int, arrow_color: int, direction: str) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:339:        p[1 + dr, 1 + dc] = arrow_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:571:def _place_arrow_source(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:574:    arrow_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:585:        patch = _make_arrow_patch(border_color, arrow_color, target_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:664:    if not _place_arrow_source(input_grid, border_colors[2], source_colors[0], 0, dest_centers):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:666:    if not _place_arrow_source(input_grid, border_colors[3], source_colors[1], 1, dest_centers):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:3:# Change: 黑色边框矩形容器，内部为灰色/橙色填充，附带同色头部线段指示方向... → 头部为箭头形状而非线段\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:20:# - The moving marker is no longer a 1-cell-thick line. It is a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:25:# - The destination marker is an identical arrow sprite of the same color, translated further\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:26:#   along the arrow's pointing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:27:# - To make \"direction from shape\" necessary, the arrow is attached only to a side orthogonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:32:#   Variant logic: an arrow attached above may still point right, so the container moves right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:33:#   The solver must read the arrow shape, then find the matching arrow destination along that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:37:# - The arrow has only four orientations and one fixed size, so the new degree of freedom is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:47:#   the subset of pixels closest to the border. With an arrow sprite, that \"closest layer only\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:48:#   extraction would lose most of the arrow and break matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:50:#   shape, matches it against four fixed arrow templates, and derives direction from that match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:53:# - Each generated object reserves a rectangle covering: input container, input arrow, destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:54:#   arrow, moved container, and moved arrow. Reserved rectangles are packed with a 1-cell margin,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:56:# - The destination arrow is always at least one background cell away from the head arrow, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:60:# - Because the arrow is orthogonally attached, the changed mechanism is visible in every mover:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:65:# - Only three object types remain on the board: container, source arrow, destination arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:66:#   The arrow is compact (3x3), monochrome, and separated from other assemblies by background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:70:#   cue that the viewer has to infer is the arrow orientation itself.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:114:def _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h: int, outer_w: int, attach_side: str, anchor: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:124:def _stamp_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, tl: tuple[int, int], direction: str, color: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:141:    Move bordered containers toward same-colored arrow destinations, charging grey cells to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:144:    - The source marker is a 3x3 arrow sprite, not a line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:145:    - Direction is derived from the arrow's normalized shape, not from which side of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:146:      container the arrow touches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:147:    - The container and arrow translate toward the nearest matching arrow destination along\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:148:      the arrow direction, capped by the number of grey interior cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:342:        head_r, head_c = _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h, outer_w, attach_side, anchor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:442:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (hr, hc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:443:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (dr, dc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:474:        _stamp_arrow(expected, (nhr, nhc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D3/0/code.py:12:      - 原题把缩放后的图案对齐到目标红方块并向外盖章\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8e5c0c38/D5/0/code.py:55:      are still just \"one-column red markers\", so the rule class stays narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D3/3/code.py:48:#    - solver 假设缩放后的图案仍含红像素且砖块尺寸为正；源锚块固定 2x2，目标锚块大小取 1..4，generator 保证成立。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:3:# Change: 无符号编码——缩放因子和反射轴均从空间关系隐式推导... → 箭头标记指示反射方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:26:# - This variant adds explicit green arrow glyphs inside each non-TL quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:27:#   A right-pointing arrow means \"apply LR reflection\"; a down-pointing arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:28:#   means \"apply UD reflection\". If a quadrant shows both arrows, both flips are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:33:#   instead show a down arrow and therefore use only UD reflection; the copied motif\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:37:# - The symbol vocabulary is intentionally small: only two 3x3 arrow glyphs exist,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:48:#   anchors. With markers added, leaving `out` unchanged would leak arrows into the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:55:# - Marker arrows are placed relative to each target anchor with a one-cell gap:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:56:#   the LR arrow sits above the anchor, the UD arrow sits left of the anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:80:# - Each non-TL quadrant has one or two green arrow components and at least one arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:82:# - Each arrow glyph matches one of the two exact templates below.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:203:        assert grouped[key] >= 1, \"each non-TL quadrant must contain at least one arrow marker\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:210:    Copy the TL motif into the other quadrants, scaling by anchor size and mirroring by arrow markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:215:    - Each non-TL quadrant additionally contains one or two green arrow glyphs: a right arrow requests LR reflection, and a down arrow requests UD reflection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/1/code.py:219:    - For each target quadrant, read its arrow glyphs to decide which reflections to apply, then scale the transformed motif by the ratio between target-