y:407:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D15/2/code.py:408:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:13:#    - 为了让人类可观察，我们在真正需要拐弯的 junction cell 上放置有颜色的箭头标记：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:42:#      * 如果直接保留，会把对角箭头装饰像素也算成轨道，产生许多孤立小 component。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:45:#      * 新版必须把 turn-marker center 的颜色 4/5 也视作 wire 邻接，否则 9-rect 紧邻箭头时会漏掉面连接。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:52:#    - 主通道列全部贯通，横向 crossover row 之间至少隔 2 行；这样对角箭头装饰不会压到另一条横线。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:58:#    - 观察者能看到：原来 5 号灰色“直行夹子”消失了，取而代之的是 4/5 号彩色箭头拐角。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:60:#    - continuous vertical columns 让“为什么需要箭头”在图上可见：没有箭头时，许多 junction 明显存在直行分支。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:63:#    - 箭头装饰只占一个对角像素，不直接铺在主线中央，因此 wire 主体仍清晰。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:65:#    - 9-rect 仍保持纯色矩形块，不叠加箭头。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:69:#    - 4/5 只用于箭头，不与 token 复用；解题者无需猜测颜色置换。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:243:    At a marked junction, the color+diagonal arrow selects a corner pair and overrides\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:320:    Send each token through the cyan network, but read colored arrow junctions before deciding where to turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:324:    - The wire system uses color 8 for ordinary pipe, color 9 for pass-through blocks, and colors 4/5 for turn-marker junction cells plus their diagonal arrow decoration.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:333:    - Continuous channel columns make many junctions ambiguous, so the correct route comes from decoding the local arrow markers, not from a generic straight-ahead heuristic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:593:    at those cells the tracer can keep going straight unless it reads the local arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/0/code.py:338:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/0/code.py:339:    remove = int(n - narrow_w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D13/1/code.py:96:    - The marker size is a decoy: the real motion size comes from the endpoint river pads, so chokepoints narrower than the decoded n still block the move.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D13/1/code.py:246:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D13/1/code.py:247:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D8/2/code.py:111:    - A single full-height grey (5) separator column splits the grid into a wide left pane and a narrow right pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:21:#      placement before a narrow gate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:135:    Key insight: The border marker decides role assignment, while chokepoints narrower than n still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:333:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D16/1/code.py:334:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D13/2/code.py:143:    - If a choke in the river is narrower than n, the mover instead stops at the farthest reachable placement, and its start area turns blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D13/2/code.py:292:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D13/2/code.py:293:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D5/4/code.py:65:   - Humans can see the rule from 2-4 examples because output becomes a narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/0/code.py:33:#   therefore mirrored too: left becomes the narrow ray zone, right becomes the wide sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/0/code.py:115:    - A full-height grey (5) separator column splits a narrow left pane from a wider right pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D10/3/code.py:78:    - A single full-height grey column splits the board into a left sprite pane and a narrow right pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/0/code.py:51:#    - Chokepoints for stuck scenes must narrow the river below square width while keeping the blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/0/code.py:321:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/0/code.py:322:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/1/code.py:30:#    - A pure row/column swap would make the grid too narrow for 2-5 side-by-side sprites if\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/1/code.py:53:#    - Bottom pane height is kept in 2-4 rows, mirroring the original narrow \"receiving\" side and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/0/code.py:37:#     - 轨迹只覆盖 mover 经过的占位区域, 不额外画箭头、数字或噪声标记.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/0/code.py:299:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/0/code.py:300:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/1/code.py:102:    - If a chokepoint narrower than n blocks the route, the black square stops at the farthest reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/1/code.py:314:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/1/code.py:315:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D3/0/code.py:58:#    narrow-hole emitters keep the alternating gap pattern. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D3/0/code.py:18:  sprites belonging to frame i are scattered only in the narrow band aligned with that frame:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/3/code.py:93:    - If the destination is blocked by a narrow section, the mover stops at the farthest reachable placement, the red destination stays, and the start area becomes river.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/3/code.py:294:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/3/code.py:295:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/2/code.py:287:    - Move the square along a shortest 4-neighbor placement path to the destination; if the destination is blocked by a narrow choke, stop at the farthest reachable placement instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/2/code.py:396:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D3/2/code.py:397:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D3/1/code.py:47:#     - every generated sample contains at least one narrow-hole emitter and one wide-hole emitter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D3/2/code.py:109:    - Rectangle size still narrows the search, but repeated slot sizes are disambiguated by the guide pixels already shown inside each hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/2/code.py:160:    - If that merge slot is unreachable because the river narrows too much, the mover stops at the farthest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/2/code.py:305:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/2/code.py:306:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D6/1/code.py:18:#     layout: one separator column still splits the board into a wide left pane and narrow right pane\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D12/2/code.py:133:    - Size no longer determines a unique slot by itself; it only narrows the search to a repeated-size group.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D14/1/code.py:97:    Slide mini black sprites into a narrow left slot, then project long red rays rightward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D14/1/code.py:119:        f\"expected narrow-left / wide-right panes, got left_w={sep}, right_w={right_w}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D2/1/code.py:290:    alignment key. Shape and symmetry narrow the options, and the anchor markers finish the match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D4/1/code.py:12:#         and drawn from a narrow zigzag family, so the frame bitmap itself is symmetric across both axes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/0/code.py:19:# - Complexity calibration: restricting to a single cycle could become too narrow if the cycle order\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D2/2/code.py:55:      单像素标记既能肉眼看出差异，又不会把输入变成复杂箭头语法。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:33:#       narrow: width == 1, stays blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:38:#     - recolor only wide frames to teal (8); narrow frames remain blue (1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:50:#   - Every sample contains both narrow and wide frames, so the blue/teal split is observable in 2-3 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:56:#     That becomes wrong here because all frames have holes but narrow ones must stay blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:145:    - Recolor only wide frames (thickness >= 2) to teal (8); narrow one-pixel frames stay blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:242:    num_narrow = random.randint(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[0], min(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[1], num_components - 1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:248:    thicknesses = [NARROW_THICKNESS] * num_narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:249:    thicknesses.extend(random.choice(wide_choices) for _ in range(num_components - num_narrow))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:225:    Add red outlines around objects, and also treat deep narrow indentations as holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:229:    - Some objects have true enclosed holes; others may instead have a narrow deep notch that opens to the outside from one side of the object's tight bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:233:    - If a component has either enclosed holes or deep narrow boundary indentations, recolor the component to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D1/3/code.py:14:#    - The comb/bracket structures stay unchanged: a single opening side leads into a narrow cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D11/1/code.py:49:#    Cluster-local columns are narrow and outlines stay disjoint, so there is no dense overlap of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:9:#     - The D11 change is a single-color thin arrow placed in the open corridor between those two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:10:#       training frames. The arrow is horizontal or vertical and points from source frame to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:19:#         - solver locates the arrow component in the gap between those two frames\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:20:#         - arrow tip decides which frame is destination, so only one direction is inferred\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:22:#       - horizontal arrow = 1-pixel shaft plus a 3-pixel head inside the frame gap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:23:#       - vertical arrow = same idea rotated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:28:#       adjacent, which makes the arrow legible and avoids diagonal-direction ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:32:#     - find_square_frames(): still valid because the arrow never touches a frame border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:33:#     - blank-frame detection: unchanged; the arrow lives outside all interiors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:37:#       assumption is removed. The new code assumes a unique arrow component exists in the pair gap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:39:#       and enough empty corridor cells for the arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:43:#     - The arrow is drawn strictly inside the corridor between the two training frames, so it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:46:#     - A human can spot the source->destination relation directly from the arrow before reasoning\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:51:#     - No region mixes multiple overlays: background first, then frames, then the arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:52:#     - The arrow occupies only the gap between the two training frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:433:        arrow = _direction_from_component(pts, axis)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:434:        if arrow == \"right\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:436:        if arrow == \"left\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:465:    arrow = _direction_from_component(pts, axis)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:466:    if arrow == \"down\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:468:    if arrow == \"up\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:475:    Read a framed training analogy with an explicit arrow cue, then transform the test sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:481:    - A thin single-color arrow sits between the two training frames and points from the source frame to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:485:    - Match the two training frames by their interior color set, then decode the arrow to decide which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:493:      the arrow marker, so the solver must parse that cue before learning the sprite rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:862:def draw_direction_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:1016:    draw_direction_arrow(grid, src_box, dst_box, marker_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:25:#     - Variant: the matched red is intentionally narrower than the socket, so the old sweep would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:54:#       identical to the old narrow trail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:9:#    - 本变体把“空框”改成“提示框”：它的内部用保留色 7 画一支 8 向箭头，箭头表示训练对的有向关系，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:11:#    - 具体小例子：若两个同配色训练框分别位于左上和右下，提示框中的箭头若指向右下，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:12:#      则 solver 必须把左上当源、右下当目标；若箭头反向，则应交换两者。原始 solver 会双向尝试再打分，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:13:#      变体 solver 则先读箭头，再只按箭头指定方向推断模板并作用到测试框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:17:#      （如镜像、自反反色），即使有箭头也不会改变测试输出，会退化回原题。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:25:#    - 提示箭头只画在提示框内部，并且保留色 7 不出现在训练/测试精灵、边框和背景中，避免识别冲突。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:27:#    - 人类看到样例时，可以先注意到唯一的保留色箭头，再观察它指向哪一个训练框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:30:#    - 箭头只占提示框内部，不叠加到其他对象上；背景和边框颜色与提示色、精灵色相互避让。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:375:def arrow_mask(n: int, direction: tuple[int, int]) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:399:    return arrow_mask(n, direction) * HINT_COLOR\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:407:        if np.array_equal(mask, arrow_mask(inner.shape[0], direction)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:447:    - The remaining frame is no longer empty: it contains a color-7 arrow that points from the training source frame toward the training destination frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:450:    - Detect the hint frame by its reserved arrow color, decode the arrow direction, and use that direction to order the two matched training frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:455:    - The extra frame is now active metadata: it tells you how to read the analogy, not what to draw directly. The puzzle is “arrow says A -> B, so apply the same rule to C”.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:3:# Change: 网格边缘的单个绿色像素作为路径起点，向网格内部延伸... → L形/箭头形绿色标记作为起点，并由其形状编码初始方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:21:#     variant: a 3-pixel green arrowhead/V marker:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:29:#       - the arrowhead orientation, not border contact alone, determines the main travel direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:37:#       - inside that component, the unique degree-2 cell is the arrow tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:65:#   - humans can read the marker as an arrowhead/V immediately; there is no hidden color-id convention\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:71:#   - that component forms a valid arrowhead with one degree-2 tip and two symmetric wing cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:76:    \"\"\"Return (start_row, start_col, init_dir) from a 3-pixel arrowhead marker.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:93:    assert len(tips) == 1 and len(wings) == 2, \"green marker must be an arrowhead\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:109:    - The path source is a 3-pixel green arrowhead near one border, not a single pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:110:    - The arrowhead's orientation encodes the path's initial direction; its interior tip is the actual start cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:113:    - Decode the arrowhead direction from its shape, then aim for the opposite grid edge along that axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:129:    # --- decode the unique green arrowhead marker ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D2/1/code.py:49:#     - Pixel-wise, the input shows only a narrow band cut from the motif, embedded inside a uniform padding color on a 20x20 canvas: for example a 4x18 row strip or an 18x4 column strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D2/1/code.py:67:#     - Humans can see the D2 change immediately because the input is no longer a block-like patch; it is a long narrow slice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D2/1/code.py:176:    - The non-padding strip is extremely elongated: a narrow horizontal band or a narrow vertical band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D2/1/code.py:185:    - The visible evidence is only a narrow band, so the meaningful support is the extracted strip rather than the whole padded canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:18:#      enters a progressively narrower corridor and draws nested rectangular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:61:#      path's layer-by-layer penetration into a narrowing channel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:189:    - Use the border-colored cells to recover the rectangular in-bounds part of the crop, which reveals which sides of the 20x20 support were crossed and sharply narrows the allowed source offsets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dd6b8c4b/D7/1/code.py:47:#    Trails occupy narrow corridors outside the destination block and do not overlap the destination or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D3/2/code.py:56:#      narrow corner footprint. The workspace remains mostly open, so the panel and the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"com